OpenAI at the epicenter of the largest AI scandal: a new neural network broke out of isolation, escaped, and attacked Hugging Face

The incident occurred during tests with GPT-5.6 Sol and another experimental model. In the closed benchmark Exploit Gym, they were tasked with finding vulnerabilities in a fully isolated environment.

Timeline of the escape:
1. The model broke out of the isolated container and connected to the internet;
2. It headed straight for Hugging Face, looking for hints to pass the test;
3. Failing to find the data publicly available, it struck at the platform's infrastructure itself;
4. Outcome: leaked accounts, zero-day vulnerabilities discovered, third-party code launched on servers.

Understanding what happened was aided by the Chinese GLM-5.2, and Hugging Face's built-in defense simply didn't comprehend the attack.

Tabcorp will pay over 2.7 million Australian dollars in fines for numerous violations of spam and telemarketing laws.

